<task id="095" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Submit Invoice from the Outlook add-in: POST /api/finance/invoice-submissions/from-email (email-only save + submission)</title>
    <phase>3 Procedures and files (WP3, EB-D-148) — wave W3-F</phase>
    <gate>blocked until 094 and 088 are done AND #2177 (task 130, T8) is merged and deployed to dev</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New authorized BFF endpoint (tags bff-api, auth) that writes an own-Restricted .eml and a submission all or nothing; tenant-isolation marker with an ArchTest.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Auth and isolation (own-Restricted .eml, submission marker, (a′) interplay), .eml resolution across duplicate paths and retryable vs permanent refusals; a cross-project contract with word-add-in-r1.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P3-F</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Shares InvoiceSubmissionContracts.cs and InvoiceSubmissionService.cs with 097 (correction mode); run 095 and 097 one after the other.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>094, 088</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, auth, finance, office, write-path, secure-records</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Build the from-email endpoint exactly as model section 9.1 "Email-only save" specifies: one call saves the email as its .eml Document (no attachment Documents) through the existing /office/save pipeline, own-Restricted with the submission marker in the same create, resolves that .eml from its communication, and submits the marked Invoice attachment (plus Supporting files) through 094's Submit Invoice operation, all or nothing. The submission job reads the marked parts' bytes out of the saved .eml in SPE, app-only.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the Office save pipeline (OfficeService, UploadFinalizationWorker), Minimal API filters, Dataverse access narrowing (uac-r2 D7) and idempotent intake. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>POST /api/finance/invoice-submissions/from-email exists in the /api/finance group with every filter 9.1 names; a valid request leaves exactly one own-Restricted, marked .eml linked to its communication and one submission naming it; every refusal leaves neither; an ArchTest pins the marker's only writer.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>The contract is projects/ebilling-r1/notes/procedure-and-file-model.md section 9.1, "Surfaces" through "Why one call, not two", and the (a′) bullet "On an add-in invoice"; reviews sections 4.x, 14, 15. Code (verified 2026-10-21; lines drift): save route filters Api/Office/OfficeEndpoints.cs:185-195; EntityAccessFilter reads only a SaveRequest argument (Api/Filters/EntityAccessFilter.cs:347-358); OfficeService.SaveAsync (:365), per-user duplicate FindExistingAsync (:423) and early return (:433-447), save key GenerateIdempotencyKey (:1194-1204; the model's :1239-1249 is stale), capture before upload (:498-517); SelectedAttachmentFileNames null = all, [] = none (Workers/Office/UploadFinalizationWorker.cs:1033-1045); IsEmailArchive set at OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs:327 and UploadFinalizationWorker.cs:684; GetEmailArchiveByCommunicationAsync returns the first only (src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:1152); .eml parts exist only for attachments sent with ContentBase64 (OfficeEmailEnricher.cs:324); AccessInheritance.OwnNarrowing (Services/Access/SecureRootInheritance.Cascade.cs:368). 088 adds the marker column on sprk_document. #2177 moves the .eml-to-communication link into the create; on this branch it is still best-effort after the create (OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs:330-338).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/InvoiceSubmissionFromEmailEndpoint.cs (route, filters; name directional)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/FromEmailSubmissionService.cs (marks, bytes, save, .eml resolution, A, submission; name directional)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeService.cs, OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs (submission-path create option: own Restricted + marker; in-process .eml id)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs, IDocumentDataverseService.cs (list variant of the email-archive lookup)</file>
      <file role="modify">Services/Finance/Submission/InvoiceSubmissionContracts.cs; Services/Jobs/Handlers/InvoiceSubmissionProcessingJobHandler.cs (byte read from the .eml); Infrastructure/DI/FinanceModule.cs and the Finance endpoint-mapping call site</file>
      <file role="new">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/SubmissionMarkerWriterGuardTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Finance/Submission/FromEmailSubmissionServiceTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/Finance/InvoiceSubmissionFromEmailContractTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 Marks">Each named attachment is Invoice (exactly one), Supporting or Don't save; any other value, zero or two Invoice marks, or a mark on an inline part → 400 before any write. A mark identifies an attachment by file name, size and content type as sent. Invoice → Stored File Invoice PDF; Supporting → Invoice supporting file; both Firm-visible No; Don't save creates nothing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 step 0">Before any write, every Invoice and Supporting attachment must be present with its ContentBase64; otherwise 422 naming the file.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 step 1 (uac-r2 F2-a)">The server overwrites SelectedAttachmentFileNames with [] whatever the client sends (null means every attachment). The save runs through the existing /office/save pipeline in-process.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 Route and filters (uac-r2 F2-a)">The route is in the /api/finance group: step 0 (099) before any record read, then OfficeAuthFilter, EntityAccessFilter (Read and AppendTo on the target core record), the Office Save rate limit and OfficeVersionSaveAuthorizationFilter, plus RequireEbillingEnabled. Core record types: sprk_matter, sprk_project, sprk_workassignment (the FilingCores list, never sprk_matter alone).</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 step 1a (uac-r2 F2-b, v5.7 change 3)">The .eml is resolved from its communication, never from a returned or job-result document id. Fresh create: the .eml this request created (in-process; no search). Duplicate path: candidates are Documents with that sprk_relatedcommunication AND sprk_isemailarchive = true, filed under the target core record with no parent document, created by the caller only; if more than one, the one whose MIME parts contain the Invoice mark's SHA-256. A then runs through the refile path; a communication filed elsewhere → 409 document_core_record_mismatch.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 F1-c (owner v5.7)">The email that can't be identified is refused and nothing is saved (no .eml, no submission); never task 130's save-Restricted fallback. Retryable ("try again", 503): Graph timeout, Graph 429, Graph 5xx, transient Dataverse error. Permanent (named, non-retryable, suggests the internal upload route): no Message-ID; Graph 403 or 404; a duplicate onto an earlier unlinked or task-130 Restricted .eml; no communication resolves; none or several candidates after the SHA check.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 own-Restricted (owner F1-a (i), uac-r2 v5.7 change 1)">An .eml this endpoint creates is saved with AccessInheritance.OwnNarrowing(Restricted) and the submission marker in the SAME create, written only by this submission path. An .eml resolved from an earlier normal save is neither narrowed nor marked. The marker is never written in any update payload.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 step 2 (uac-r2 F1-b)">The submission names the .eml as its source document and each marked attachment by file name and SHA-256, matched against the .eml's MIME parts; it refuses when no communication resolves.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 step 3 (uac-r2 F2-c)">The job starts only after the .eml's finalization and reads bytes from the saved .eml in SPE app-only, never a mailbox: one retrieve of the .eml row gives driveId, itemId and versionnumber; the part's ordinal, name and SHA-256 must match the mark or the submission ends Failed; step 4's IfRowVersionMatches pins that version. Logs carry ids and ordinals only, never file names or subjects. A failed .eml finalization ends the submission Failed; the .eml survives a failed submission.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 Idempotency key">Message-ID + core record + mode + invoice id + the sorted (file name, mark) list; a different marking is a different operation. Mode values: New, and Correction with a required invoice id (400 when missing); 097 implements Correction in the operation, this task only carries it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">BFF hygiene per .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md: placement stated, publish-size delta against a fresh master build, no new package, no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="live data">No live Dataverse writes and no deploys.</constraint>
    <constraint source="095 contract, pinned 2026-10-27 for word-add-in-r1">The wire contract in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/095-from-email-contract.md (request fields, idempotency rule, 202 body, replay rules, error statuses and codes) is binding. Any change to it, including resolving its open points OP-1 to OP-8, needs word-add-in-r1's agreement before it merges. word-add-in-r1 AGREED the whole file (sections 1-9, OP-1 to OP-8) at 717cf238d9 on 2026-10-27; their task 133 builds against it. EB-D-160 (re-attempt after Failed) was added after that agreement and is sent to them.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
