    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Column-writer ArchTest with must-fire / must-not-fire controls" location="tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/DocumentAccessPermissionWriterGuardTests.cs">Copy its source scan, member attribution, approved-writer list and Detector_MustFireAndMustNotFire controls for the marker column; add an update-payload ban.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare FULL. Confirm the gate: #2177 merged into this branch (the .eml-to-communication link is written in the create) and deployed to dev; else STOP. Read 088's marker column and 094's operation.</step>
    <step order="1">Request model and route: email payload (as /office/save), core record, marks, mode, invoice id, client idempotency key; filters in the constrained order; make EntityAccessFilter see the target (a SaveRequest argument or an extension of its extraction).</step>
    <step order="2">Service: marks validation (400), bytes-present (422), [] overwrite, in-process save with the submission-path create option (own Restricted + marker), .eml resolution (fresh / duplicate), A via the refile path, refusal classification, then 094's operation with the .eml as source.</step>
    <step order="3">List variant of the email-archive lookup; the job's byte read from the .eml's MIME parts with the F2-c checks.</step>
    <step order="4">SubmissionMarkerWriterGuardTests with must-fire and must-not-fire controls.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests per the acceptance criteria; seeding proof; build; Office, Finance and Submission unit tests; full ArchTests; publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="6">Notes in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/095-submit-invoice-from-email.md: request contract for word-add-in-r1, refusal table, seeding proof, §11 answers. Send the contract to word-add-in-r1.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` after the adversarial reviews and uac-r2's review.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If #2177 is not merged into this branch and deployed to dev, STOP: from-email does not ship before it (model 9.1 Prerequisite).</trigger>
    <trigger>If the own-Restricted narrowing and the marker cannot be written in the .eml's create (only in a later update), STOP and report; do not write the marker in an update.</trigger>
    <trigger>If word-add-in-r1's request shape differs from 9.1 (marks keyed other than file name + size + content type, or "add supporting files to an existing invoice" sent through this route), STOP and settle the contract; the model routes supporting files for an existing invoice through the internal upload route.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>POST /office/save (OfficeEndpoints.cs:185) saves the email; 094's Submit Invoice operation submits a source Document; GetEmailArchiveByCommunicationAsync (DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:1152) finds the first .eml of a communication.</existing>
    <extension>The save pipeline and 094's operation are reused in-process, not copied. A separate route is required: /office/save's replay and duplicate keys cannot carry a submission (OfficeService.cs:1194-1204) and two client calls can leave an email saved with no submission (model 9.1). The lookup gets a list variant because one communication can have several .eml Documents after #2177.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The add-in's Invoice module has no server call: an invoice arriving by email in Outlook cannot be submitted, and the word-add-in-r1 contract (owner I, L) fails.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build, test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">InvoiceSubmissionFromEmailEndpoint.cs; FromEmailSubmissionService.cs; OfficeService / OfficeDocumentPersistence create option; email-archive list lookup; job byte read</output>
    <output type="test">SubmissionMarkerWriterGuardTests.cs; FromEmailSubmissionServiceTests.cs; InvoiceSubmissionFromEmailContractTests.cs</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/095-submit-invoice-from-email.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Happy path: one call creates one .eml Document (sprk_isemailarchive true, linked to its communication, filed under the core record, own Restricted, marker set) with no attachment child Documents, and one submission naming it; the job stages the Invoice and Supporting parts as Stored Files (Firm-visible No) and the invoice is created (test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Marks: zero or two Invoice marks, an unknown mark value, or a mark on an inline part → 400; an Invoice or Supporting attachment without bytes → 422 naming the file; each writes nothing (tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A client-sent SelectedAttachmentFileNames of null or a non-empty list is overwritten with [] (test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Filters: unauthenticated → 401; flagged-external caller → refused by step 0 before any record read; caller without Read and AppendTo on the core record → 403 from EntityAccessFilter; rate limit exceeded → 429; eBilling off → 503 ebilling.disabled (tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Duplicate path: a second call by the same user for the same email and record resolves the caller's own .eml from the communication (never from a job result); another user's marked .eml of the same email is never chosen; several of the caller's candidates are narrowed by the Invoice SHA-256; none or still several → the permanent refusal (tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An .eml resolved from an earlier normal save is neither narrowed nor marked; a communication filed to another core record → 409 document_core_record_mismatch (tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Refusals save nothing (no .eml, no submission): Graph timeout, 429, 5xx and a transient Dataverse error → retryable 503; no Message-ID, Graph 403 or 404, a duplicate onto an unlinked or task-130 Restricted .eml, no communication → permanent named refusals (one test each).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Job byte read: a part whose ordinal, name or SHA-256 differs from the mark ends the submission Failed; the .eml survives; logs carry no file name or subject (tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Idempotency: the same key returns the earlier result and creates nothing; a different marking or mode is a different operation; mode Correction without an invoice id → 400 (tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ArchTest: the marker column is written only by the submission create path, only in the create that writes the narrowing, never in an update payload; must-fire controls (a writer in another member; the marker in an update payload) and must-not-fire controls (the approved create; a read) pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Seeding proof, recorded in notes: add a marker write to an update payload → the ArchTest fails; restored.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; Office, Finance and Submission unit tests, contract tests and the full ArchTests pass (known pre-existing failures listed by name); publish-size delta recorded; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Contract tests (InvoiceSubmissionFromEmailContractTests.cs) pin the request and response field names, the status codes and the errorCode / reasonCode values listed in notes/095-from-email-contract.md, one test per error-table row and per replay row (tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Reviews: adversarial-reviewer twice (auth, tenant isolation), uac-r2, and word-add-in-r1 for the contract. Known limits (model 9.1, owner-visible): cloud-link or over-20 MB invoices cannot be submitted from the add-in; an earlier normal save with the invoice ticked leaves an invoice-PDF Document beside the Stored File; a later normal save after this call answers "already saved" (#2209); lower-then-raise of the .eml's Restricted leaves the marker. 096 removes the old Office invoice legs one release after word-add-in-r1 ships the module. word-add-in-r1 2026-10-21: the from-email request and response shapes are frozen as model §9.1 states them; any change to either is sent to word-add-in-r1 before it merges. Their add-in release (Invoice view, Submit Invoice button, Invoice removed from Save and quick-create) follows this task's dev deploy and 118's marking component; 096 is one release after it. uac-r2 2026-10-22 (round 122, #2234): a save-time "email unidentified" Restricted is PROVISIONAL (AccessInheritance.OwnNarrowingUntilEmailIdentified, written only by ApplyEmailCommunicationOutcome) and is released to the communication's value once the .eml is linked. The submission's own Restricted on the .eml must be a NON-provisional own narrowing: do not build it through ApplyEmailCommunicationOutcome's unidentified branch (own path or factory). Must-fire test: a linked submission .eml stays Restricted. ontology-r1 088 gate 2026-10-22: the .eml source is held by sprk_storedfile.sprk_sourcedocument and sprk_sourcecommunication (Restrict). 094 extends the document delete 409 pre-check to count Stored File references; this task confirms that it covers the .eml document this route creates (must-fire test: deleting the submission's .eml returns 409 and the SPE file is untouched). The communication side follows 117's rule.</notes>

